\begin{proof}
By definition, the problems in (\ref{eq:LagFun}) and (\ref{eq:SecondLevel}) are primal/dual problems.  The primal problem always has an optimal solution because it is bounded. Since Problem OPT-rPS is an LP problem, the relaxed dual problem is also bounded and feasible. Therefore the relaxed dual problem also has an optimal solution.  We have the {\em strong duality} if the primal problem is convex, which is the case here since Problem OPT-rPS is an LP problem. 
\end{proof}

We have Theorem~\ref{th:th2} on the optimality of the path selection solution, which follows naturally from Lemmas~\ref{lemma:1} and~\ref{lemma:2}.
